{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Prompts that follow your mood (1.4 E; specs/1.4-features.md §E, UX 18 Nov). On Write, above an empty entry. flagged (an entry or tag today that the crisis matcher flags): no prompt at all. No check-in today (mood null): prompts.json's daily prompt, daily[dayNumber(today) mod N], Another stepping through the daily list. With today's check-in mood (its current value; an edit later that day moves the group): mood 1-2 hard-days, 3 noticing, 4-5 gratitude. Free: one prompt a day, group[dayNumber(today) mod group length]; Another falls back to the daily list from the day's own prompt (another=1) on, never a second group prompt. Plus: group[(place + another) mod length], savedPlace = place + another (the library's per-group place on the device). help: the group's help (hard-days true): Get help now under the prompt, never counted. dayNumber: days since 1970-01-01 of the profile's date (YYYY-MM-DD), not UTC. No new analytics: prompt_used stays a name only. Generated by scripts/gen-mood-prompts-contract.mjs from the two prompt lists alone.",
  "rules": {
    "moodGroup": {
      "1": "hard-days",
      "2": "hard-days",
      "3": "noticing",
      "4": "gratitude",
      "5": "gratitude"
    }
  },
